# Design system tokens standard

## Source of truth

- App styling tokens are the primary API and must be defined under `src/styles/design-tokens.css`.
- Token families include:
  - colors (`--app-color-*`)
  - typography (`--app-font-*`, `--app-type-*`)
  - spacing (`--app-space-*`)
  - radius/borders (`--app-radius-*`, `--app-border-*`)
  - shadows (`--app-shadow-*`)

## Angular Material integration

- `src/material-theme.scss` is the only theme bridge for Angular Material token integration.
- Material/MDC override variables (`--mat-sys-*`, `--mdc-*`) are allowed only in `src/material-theme.scss`.
- Feature, layout, and component styles must consume app tokens (`--app-*`) instead of direct third-party tokens.

## Component styling requirements

- In `src/app/**`, avoid hardcoded spacing/radius/shadow values when a token exists.
- Use semantic app tokens (for example `--app-color-primary-soft`) instead of one-off color math whenever possible.
- Keep Material component overrides narrow and reusable via global bridge classes in `src/material-theme.scss`.

## Tailwind usage

- Keep Tailwind theme values aligned to app tokens through `src/styles.css` `@theme inline`.
- Utility classes and SCSS should reference the same token scales for spacing, radius, color, typography, and shadows.
